# Supabase (GNO)

## Schema

- Migrations only under `supabase/migrations/` — no ad-hoc prod DDL from the app.
- Primary keys and uniqueness must match ingested Amazon report identities (composite keys when needed).
- Document non-obvious columns in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.

## Access

- Server uses service role / local client via a single supabase module.
- Repositories own queries; services do not embed raw SQL/filters except through the repository.
- Prefer upsert with clear conflict targets matching migration constraints.

## Local

- Each tool has its own Supabase ports — do not collide with sibling tools.
- Reset/migrate via project scripts; keep sample data paths under `reports/` or documented fixtures.
